"react": "^16.11.0"

**Describe the issue**
Right now, axios helpfully copies its config into all error messages. Unfortunately, if there is sensitive data in this config (e.g. API keys) this is also logged. There should be an easily accessible option to help prevent this, because most people won't bother to put in the effort for security. This use case is intended for node.js users, where consumers of the logs aren't necessarily as privileged as those running the library.

**Example Code**
