When a JSON response contains big numbers, we lose some precision in the number.  E.g:
```
{ "data": 1000000000000100000001 }
```
becomes
```
{ "data": 1.0000000000001e+21 }
```
which equals 1000000000000100000000

#### Current workaround
My current workaround is to implement my own response transformation that uses `json-bigint` to do the parsing like so:
```
function transform(data) {
            // Replacing the default transformResponse in axios because this uses JSON.parse and causes problems
            // with precision of big numbers.
            // https://github.com/axios/axios/blob/6642ca9aa1efae47b1a9d3ce3adc98416318661c/lib/defaults.js#L57
            /* eslint no-param-reassign:0 */
            if (typeof data === 'string') {
                try {
                    data = JSONBig.parse(data);
                } catch (e) { /* Ignore */ }
            }
            return data;
        }
```

It would be great if this was the default behavior of Axios.

